I would call it an Interactive Online Exam Sheet or, more specifically, an Interactive Exam Practice Form.

The version I generated is a dynamic, fillable form embedded directly in the ChatGPT conversation. It includes multiple-choice checkboxes, dropdown selections, and text fields where you can type your answers.

A few useful terms:

- Interactive exam sheet — the general name for the whole exercise.
- Fillable online exam — emphasizes that you can enter answers directly.
- Interactive quiz — particularly suitable for multiple-choice questions and automatic scoring.
- Web-based exam simulator — suggests a more complete practice environment with a timer, scoring, and feedback.

For our Advanced Machine Learning preparation, I'd call it the Advanced Machine Learning Interactive Exam Simulator.

One important distinction: the current form lets you enter answers, but it does not yet automatically grade them or guarantee that your answers will be saved outside the conversation. We could develop it into a more complete simulator with a 90-minute timer, mark allocation, model answers, and feedback for each question.
